# Ocentra Parent Rule Index

Read this file before coding in this repo. It is a router, not the whole rulebook.

## Core Rule

Do not add product behavior until the relevant scaffold boundary exists, is typed, and is validated.

## Always Read

- `.ocentra-ai/rules/ocentra-parent-validation.mdc`
- `.ocentra-ai/rules/ocentra-parent-source-shape.mdc`
- `.ocentra-ai/rules/ocentra-parent-domain-boundaries.mdc`

## Task Routing

| If touching | Read this first |
| --- | --- |
| Tests, test helpers, smoke checks | `.ocentra-ai/rules/ocentra-parent-test-rules.mdc` |
| Effect Schema, brands, constants, package contracts | `.ocentra-ai/rules/ocentra-parent-domain-boundaries.mdc` |
| Endpoints, local API paths, WebSocket commands/events | `.ocentra-ai/rules/ocentra-parent-protocol-websocket.mdc` |
| Rust crates or localhost service code | `.ocentra-ai/rules/ocentra-parent-rust-service.mdc` |
| Vite portal UI or browser transport | `.ocentra-ai/rules/ocentra-parent-portal.mdc` |
| Logs, telemetry, diagnostics, redaction | `.ocentra-ai/rules/ocentra-parent-logging-redaction.mdc` |
| Auth, localhost trust, child-device safety, abuse cases | `.ocentra-ai/rules/ocentra-parent-security-localhost.mdc` |
| File size, function size, module ownership | `.ocentra-ai/rules/ocentra-parent-source-shape.mdc` |
| CI, local validation, build gates | `.ocentra-ai/rules/ocentra-parent-validation.mdc` |

## Precedence

1. `AGENTS.md`
2. This `.ocentra-ai/rules` index and its routed rule files
3. Existing local package/crate patterns
4. User direction in the current thread

If two rules conflict, stop and resolve the conflict before editing.

## Do Not Blindly Import Old Ocentra Games Rules

`E:\ocentra-games\.cursor` is reference material from that project. Ocentra Parent keeps its own tool-neutral `.ocentra-ai` guidance and has different boundaries:

- local Windows Rust service first
- Vite dev portal first
- Cloudflare later
- no game economy
- no Solana assumptions
- no product capture or parental-control enforcement until explicitly planned
